I'm having trouble tracking down why allocating a new thread at run time is causing a deadlock. I am tempted to instead just check the project settings when initializing the WTP and allocate enough for one thread per system. I.e.:

```
int minimum_threads = 1;
minimum_threads += bool(GLOBAL_GET("physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread"))? 1:0;
minimum_threads += bool(GLOBAL_GET("physics/2d/run_on_separate_thread"))? 1:0;
minimum_threads += OS::get_singleton()->is_separate_thread_rendering_enabled()? 1:0;
minimum_threads += bool(GLOBAL_GET("rendering/textures/vram_compression/compress_with_gpu"))? 1:0; // No guarantee that Betsy is used, but this is the best we can do
```

What do you think?

