@bruvzg @Ivorforce This is my hack to ensure that the LocalVector is never resized at run time. Personally, I think this is a bit brittle, but I'm not sure what else to do. Reading from the project settings like I suggested above seems equally brittle to me. 

One option that may be a bit safer would be to do this change, but use a FixedVector instead of a LocalVector, then if we ever try to allocate more threads than those reserved, we will get a very clear error and it will be easy to trace back the issue to the number of threads reserved. 

What do you think?

